  "query_preview": "..\nIssued at 135 PM CDT Sun Aug 30 2026\n\nA potent upper level ridge is slowly working its way over the area \ntoday and tomorrow and will remain overhead through the end of the \nwork week. Another day of deep mixing today is leading to dewpoints \nin the lower to mid 60s and highs in the mid 90s. Southerly return \nflow on Monday brings a modest increase in moisture with dewpoints \ncloser to 70 for the remainder of the week. Monday also kicks off \nanother heatwave that lasts all week with limited relief by the \nweekend. \n\nHeat indices are expected to climb to 100+ degrees Monday through \nFriday with the potential for some areas to see a heat index of 105 \nTuesday through Friday. Overnight lows will be in record warm low \nterritory in the mid 70s. A Heat Advisory is in effect for Monday \narea wide for the start of the prolonged heatwave. An Excessive Heat \nWatch is in effect Tuesday through Friday and may need to be \nupgraded to a Warning should confidence increase in more sites \nhitting a heat index of 105 for four days in a row. However, a key \ndifference between this heatwave and the last one is the drier \nairmass this time around. NBM max temps and heat indices have \ntrended up the last few runs with the lower dewpoints, compared to \nlast time where max temps trended down as we approached the event \nwith much higher dewpoints. The LREF probabilities of heat indices \nof 100+ degrees have increased to 80-100% Tuesday through Friday. \n\nThe EC and GFS have come into better agreement with the ridge \nshifting back west over the Plains starting Friday and continuing \nthrough the weekend. This brings only limited relief from the heat \nthough with NBM showing an isolated 20-30% chance of showers/storms \nFriday and an isolated 15-20% chance on Saturday. Highs will likely \ncontinue to be in the lower 90s through the end of the weekend.",
